1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,008
What's today's video about? It's about Japan's World Heritage Sites!

2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Nara's New World Heritage Sites

3
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:15,041
Oh, check out the news on TV!

4
00:00:15,064 --> 00:00:17,630
What's the news about?

5
00:00:17,653 --> 00:00:20,387
It's about Nara.

6
00:00:20,410 --> 00:00:25,776
Asuka and Fujiwara are now new World Heritage Sites!

7
00:00:25,799 --> 00:00:27,735
Really?

8
00:00:27,759 --> 00:00:30,559
That's amazing!

9
00:00:30,582 --> 00:00:35,182
Yeah, I'm so happy!

10
00:00:35,205 --> 00:00:40,038
Nara has so many World Heritage Sites, doesn't it?

11
00:00:40,061 --> 00:00:43,346
How many are there now?

12
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:47,906
Well, there are three right now.

13
00:00:47,929 --> 00:00:49,963
Three?

14
00:00:49,987 --> 00:00:51,801
Where are they?

15
00:00:51,824 --> 00:00:55,258
The first one is Horyu-ji Temple.

16
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:59,414
It's the oldest wooden temple in Japan.

17
00:00:59,438 --> 00:01:01,485
I see.

18
00:01:01,509 --> 00:01:04,942
I've seen it on TV before.

19
00:01:04,965 --> 00:01:09,622
The second is Nara's city area, including Todai-ji Temple.

20
00:01:09,646 --> 00:01:13,379
There's the giant Buddha statue, right?

21
00:01:13,402 --> 00:01:17,936
And there are lots of deer in the park.

22
00:01:17,959 --> 00:01:22,759
Yes, and the third is the mountains of Yoshino in the south.

23
00:01:22,782 --> 00:01:24,916
Yoshino?

24
00:01:24,939 --> 00:01:28,578
The cherry blossoms are so beautiful in spring, aren't they?

25
00:01:28,601 --> 00:01:31,268
Yes, they are.

26
00:01:31,291 --> 00:01:37,024
And with Asuka and Fujiwara this time, it'll make four!

27
00:01:37,047 --> 00:01:40,465
Does that mean Nara has the most in Japan?

28
00:01:40,489 --> 00:01:45,622
Yes, Nara is truly a special place.

29
00:01:45,645 --> 00:01:47,378
It really is.

30
00:01:47,401 --> 00:01:50,858
It has so much ancient history.

31
00:01:50,882 --> 00:01:55,515
Asuka was Japan's first major city.

32
00:01:55,538 --> 00:01:59,636
What's in Asuka now?

33
00:01:59,659 --> 00:02:03,510
There are very old temples and ancient tombs.

34
00:02:03,534 --> 00:02:05,872
Ancient tombs?

35
00:02:05,895 --> 00:02:07,946
What are those?

36
00:02:07,969 --> 00:02:12,569
They're the graves of ancient kings and important people.

37
00:02:12,592 --> 00:02:15,886
Wow, that's interesting!

38
00:02:15,910 --> 00:02:18,244
What do they look like?

39
00:02:18,267 --> 00:02:22,351
They're made with huge stones.

40
00:02:22,374 --> 00:02:26,431
Can you go inside?

41
00:02:26,455 --> 00:02:31,889
No, but you can see the wall paintings up close.

42
00:02:31,913 --> 00:02:35,368
I really want to see those paintings!

43
00:02:35,391 --> 00:02:39,726
Then how about we go together this weekend?

44
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:41,950
Sounds great!

45
00:02:41,973 --> 00:02:44,181
Let's definitely go!

46
00:02:44,204 --> 00:02:47,771
Should we take the train from Osaka?

47
00:02:47,794 --> 00:02:51,327
Yes, let's take the Kintetsu train.

48
00:02:51,350 --> 00:02:56,717
Asuka is quite spread out, so let's rent bicycles at the station.

49
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:58,706
Got it!

50
00:02:58,729 --> 00:03:01,898
Are there any restaurants with delicious food?

51
00:03:01,922 --> 00:03:07,088
Let’s try Nara’s famous persimmon leaf sushi!

52
00:03:07,111 --> 00:03:11,160
I’m so excited for our weekend trip!

53
00:03:11,184 --> 00:03:20,193
You can download today’s video script from the description and top comment. Don’t forget to leave a comment before downloading!

54
00:03:20,193 --> 00:03:21,693
Scene 2: Exploring Nara – A Visit to Todai-ji Temple

55
00:03:21,693 --> 00:03:24,526
We’ve arrived in Nara!

56
00:03:24,549 --> 00:03:27,916
Yes, the weather is perfect!

57
00:03:27,939 --> 00:03:31,272
Where should we go first?

58
00:03:31,295 --> 00:03:34,332
Let’s head to Todai-ji Temple.

59
00:03:34,356 --> 00:03:36,806
Should we walk there?

60
00:03:36,829 --> 00:03:38,429
Yes, let’s.

61
00:03:38,452 --> 00:03:42,827
It’s about a 15-minute walk from the station.

62
00:03:42,851 --> 00:03:44,851
Got it!

63
00:03:44,874 --> 00:03:46,685
Let’s go!

64
00:03:46,709 --> 00:03:49,384
Wow, there are so many people here!

65
00:03:49,407 --> 00:03:51,141
It really is.

66
00:03:51,164 --> 00:03:54,170
And lots of foreigners too.

67
00:03:54,193 --> 00:03:57,160
That’s Todai-ji Temple over there.

68
00:03:57,183 --> 00:04:01,616
Whoa, it’s such a massive building!

69
00:04:01,639 --> 00:04:05,119
Let’s go inside.

70
00:04:05,143 --> 00:04:08,076
I’ll buy the tickets.

71
00:04:08,099 --> 00:04:10,102
Thank you!

72
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:13,959
Look—it’s the Great Buddha!

73
00:04:13,982 --> 00:04:17,915
Wow, it’s really huge!

74
00:04:17,938 --> 00:04:21,871
Yes, it’s incredibly tall.

75
00:04:21,894 --> 00:04:24,970
It’s about 15 meters high!

76
00:04:24,994 --> 00:04:27,204
That’s amazing!

77
00:04:27,227 --> 00:04:29,806
Let’s take some photos.

78
00:04:29,830 --> 00:04:32,398
Okay, I’ll take one!

79
00:04:32,421 --> 00:04:35,105
Say cheese!

80
00:04:35,129 --> 00:04:37,129
Thank you!

81
00:04:37,152 --> 00:04:41,442
Next, let’s walk around the park.

82
00:04:41,465 --> 00:04:43,907
Sounds great!

83
00:04:43,930 --> 00:04:46,419
Look over there!

84
00:04:46,443 --> 00:04:51,576
Wow, there are so many deer in the park!

85
00:04:51,599 --> 00:04:53,895
They’re so cute!

86
00:04:53,919 --> 00:04:57,492
I want to feed them.

87
00:04:57,516 --> 00:05:01,360
Then let’s buy some deer crackers.

88
00:05:01,383 --> 00:05:03,717
Deer crackers?

89
00:05:03,739 --> 00:05:08,078
Yes, they’re special snacks for the deer.

90
00:05:08,102 --> 00:05:10,568
I bought one.

91
00:05:10,591 --> 00:05:12,958
Here come the deer!

92
00:05:12,981 --> 00:05:17,049
Here you go—here’s a cracker.

93
00:05:17,073 --> 00:05:19,473
They eat so eagerly!

94
00:05:19,496 --> 00:05:22,463
They’re adorable.

95
00:05:22,486 --> 00:05:25,784
Want to give them more crackers?

96
00:05:25,808 --> 00:05:29,075
Yes, let’s buy another one.

97
00:05:29,098 --> 00:05:32,031
The deer seem happy too!

98
00:05:32,054 --> 00:05:35,790
Our trip to Nara has been so much fun!

99
00:05:35,813 --> 00:05:38,413
I’m glad to hear that!

100
00:05:38,436 --> 00:05:45,541
You can review today’s video with the link in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

101
00:05:45,541 --> 00:05:47,041
Scene 3: Horyuji Temple – The World’s Oldest Wooden Structure

102
00:05:47,041 --> 00:05:50,658
We’ve arrived at Horyuji Temple!

103
00:05:50,681 --> 00:05:53,926
It’s so peaceful here.

104
00:05:53,950 --> 00:05:59,317
Yes, there are many old buildings here.

105
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:03,793
When was this temple built?

106
00:06:03,817 --> 00:06:07,017
It dates back to the Asuka period.

107
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:09,720
That’s so long ago!

108
00:06:09,743 --> 00:06:15,143
I see. It’s really ancient.

109
00:06:15,166 --> 00:06:21,900
Yes, it’s the oldest wooden building in Japan.

110
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:26,356
The oldest in Japan?

111
00:06:26,379 --> 00:06:31,984
That’s right. In fact, it’s the oldest wooden building in the world.

112
00:06:32,008 --> 00:06:37,894
The oldest in the world? That’s incredible!

113
00:06:37,918 --> 00:06:43,051
Exactly. That’s why it’s a World Heritage site.

114
00:06:43,074 --> 00:06:46,413
Let’s go inside the building.

115
00:06:46,437 --> 00:06:50,651
Sure. The entrance is over there.

116
00:06:50,674 --> 00:06:53,007
I’ve bought the tickets.

117
00:06:53,030 --> 00:06:54,797
Let’s go!

118
00:06:54,820 --> 00:07:01,440
Look! That building over there is a five-story pagoda.

119
00:07:01,463 --> 00:07:05,996
It’s so tall and beautiful!

120
00:07:06,019 --> 00:07:10,157
Yes, it’s truly stunning.

121
00:07:10,181 --> 00:07:13,756
Is it okay to take photos here?

122
00:07:13,779 --> 00:07:17,512
You can take photos outside.

123
00:07:17,535 --> 00:07:21,302
Great! Let’s take one together.

124
00:07:21,325 --> 00:07:25,599
Sure, I’ll hold the camera.

125
00:07:25,622 --> 00:07:27,389
Thank you!

126
00:07:27,412 --> 00:07:33,312
Here we go. Say cheese!

127
00:07:33,335 --> 00:07:36,968
That’s a great photo! I’m so happy.

128
00:07:36,991 --> 00:07:41,391
Next, let’s check out that building over there.

129
00:07:41,414 --> 00:07:45,666
Okay. What’s inside that one?

130
00:07:45,690 --> 00:07:48,566
There’s an ancient Buddha statue inside.

131
00:07:48,589 --> 00:07:52,272
Can I take a photo of the Buddha statue?

132
00:07:52,296 --> 00:07:58,029
No, photography isn’t allowed inside the buildings.

133
00:07:58,052 --> 00:08:01,734
Got it. I’ll be careful.

134
00:08:01,758 --> 00:08:03,892
Let’s take our time exploring.

135
00:08:03,915 --> 00:08:09,281
This Buddha statue has such a gentle face.

136
00:08:09,304 --> 00:08:13,438
Yes, I think so too.

137
00:08:13,461 --> 00:08:17,394
Horyu-ji Temple is an amazing place.

138
00:08:17,417 --> 00:08:19,750
I’m so glad we came.

139
00:08:19,773 --> 00:08:23,907
Yes, it was a great history lesson.

140
00:08:23,930 --> 00:08:28,302
Shall we go check out the souvenirs next?

141
00:08:28,325 --> 00:08:31,692
Sounds good. Let’s go!

142
00:08:31,715 --> 00:08:33,215
Scene 4: Viewing Mt. Fuji from the Shinkansen

143
00:08:33,215 --> 00:08:36,548
The Shinkansen is so fast!

144
00:08:36,571 --> 00:08:40,012
Yes, it really is.

145
00:08:40,036 --> 00:08:42,503
Oh, look!

146
00:08:42,526 --> 00:08:46,221
You can see a huge mountain out the window.

147
00:08:46,244 --> 00:08:48,244
Wow, you’re right!

148
00:08:48,267 --> 00:08:51,338
Is that Mt. Fuji?

149
00:08:51,362 --> 00:08:54,129
Yes, they are.

150
00:08:54,152 --> 00:08:57,728
It’s the most famous mountain in Japan.

151
00:08:57,751 --> 00:09:00,996
Wow, it’s so beautiful!

152
00:09:01,020 --> 00:09:03,698
The weather is perfect today.

153
00:09:03,721 --> 00:09:06,921
That’s why it’s so clear.

154
00:09:06,944 --> 00:09:10,078
The top of the mountain is white.

155
00:09:10,101 --> 00:09:13,581
Yes, because there’s snow up there.

156
00:09:13,604 --> 00:09:17,604
I want to take a photo of Mt. Fuji!

157
00:09:17,627 --> 00:09:19,260
Sounds great!

158
00:09:19,283 --> 00:09:21,898
Yes, I took it.

159
00:09:21,922 --> 00:09:24,098
That's a great photo.

160
00:09:24,122 --> 00:09:28,659
Mount Fuji is the tallest mountain in Japan.

161
00:09:28,682 --> 00:09:31,148
How tall is it?

162
00:09:31,171 --> 00:09:34,505
About 3,700 meters.

163
00:09:34,528 --> 00:09:37,012
That's really tall!

164
00:09:37,035 --> 00:09:39,924
Can you climb it?

165
00:09:39,948 --> 00:09:44,187
Yes, lots of people climb it in the summer.

166
00:09:44,210 --> 00:09:49,377
I see. I want to climb it someday too.

167
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:51,833
Do you want to climb Mount Fuji?

168
00:09:51,856 --> 00:09:55,943
Yes, I want to go all the way to the top.

169
00:09:55,966 --> 00:10:00,065
The view from the top is absolutely stunning.

170
00:10:00,088 --> 00:10:02,337
I can't wait to see it!

171
00:10:02,361 --> 00:10:05,330
It'll definitely be a wonderful memory.

172
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:08,836
But is it tough to climb?

173
00:10:08,859 --> 00:10:14,225
Yes, you walk a lot, so it's really tiring.

174
00:10:14,248 --> 00:10:18,015
Then I need to train a lot.

175
00:10:18,038 --> 00:10:22,608
Right. Good hiking shoes are important too.

176
00:10:22,631 --> 00:10:26,231
I want to buy hiking shoes.

177
00:10:26,254 --> 00:10:30,458
Great! Let's go shopping together.

178
00:10:30,482 --> 00:10:32,082
Thank you!

179
00:10:32,105 --> 00:10:36,959
There are also beautiful lakes near Mount Fuji.

180
00:10:36,983 --> 00:10:39,075
Lakes?

181
00:10:39,099 --> 00:10:43,665
Yes. The view of Mount Fuji from there is amazing.

182
00:10:43,688 --> 00:10:47,122
Then I want to visit the lakes too.

183
00:10:47,145 --> 00:10:50,811
Let's go there on our next trip.

184
00:10:50,834 --> 00:10:54,168
Yes, I'm really looking forward to it!

185
00:10:54,191 --> 00:10:55,691
Scene 5: Let's Visit Kinkaku-ji Temple

186
00:10:55,691 --> 00:10:58,630
We've arrived in Kyoto.

187
00:10:58,653 --> 00:11:01,920
Yes, it was a quick train ride.

188
00:11:01,943 --> 00:11:05,743
There are so many people here too.

189
00:11:05,766 --> 00:11:08,333
It's really lively.

190
00:11:08,356 --> 00:11:11,189
Where should we go next?

191
00:11:11,212 --> 00:11:13,979
Let's visit Kinkaku-ji.

192
00:11:14,002 --> 00:11:16,403
Kinkaku-ji?

193
00:11:16,426 --> 00:11:18,865
What kind of temple is it?

194
00:11:18,888 --> 00:11:22,855
It's a stunning golden temple.

195
00:11:22,878 --> 00:11:25,211
Golden?

196
00:11:25,234 --> 00:11:27,887
That's amazing!

197
00:11:27,911 --> 00:11:31,278
Yes, let's take the bus.

198
00:11:31,301 --> 00:11:34,787
How long does it take by bus?

199
00:11:34,810 --> 00:11:37,589
About 30 minutes.

200
00:11:37,613 --> 00:11:39,646
Got it!

201
00:11:39,669 --> 00:11:42,236
We've arrived at Kinkaku-ji!

202
00:11:42,259 --> 00:11:44,459
Let's go inside.

203
00:11:44,481 --> 00:11:46,885
I'll buy the tickets.

204
00:11:46,909 --> 00:11:48,548
Thank you!

205
00:11:48,571 --> 00:11:50,654
Look over there.

206
00:11:50,678 --> 00:11:53,745
There's a building.

207
00:11:53,768 --> 00:11:58,102
Wow, it's really golden!

208
00:11:58,125 --> 00:12:01,599
Yes, it's so beautiful.

209
00:12:01,622 --> 00:12:04,989
You can see the temple reflected in the water.

210
00:12:05,012 --> 00:12:07,869
There's a large pond, you see.

211
00:12:07,892 --> 00:12:11,226
Let's take a photo here.

212
00:12:11,249 --> 00:12:14,496
Sure, I'll take the photo.

213
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:16,093
Please do.

214
00:12:16,116 --> 00:12:19,567
The area around Kinkaku-ji is beautiful too.

215
00:12:19,590 --> 00:12:22,223
There are so many trees here.

216
00:12:22,246 --> 00:12:24,380
Let's take a walk.

217
00:12:24,403 --> 00:12:27,500
There's a souvenir shop over there.

218
00:12:27,523 --> 00:12:29,594
Let's go check it out.

219
00:12:29,618 --> 00:12:31,818
What would you like to buy?

220
00:12:31,841 --> 00:12:35,218
I'd like to get some sweets.

221
00:12:35,241 --> 00:12:38,208
Kyoto is famous for its delicious sweets.

222
00:12:38,231 --> 00:12:40,900
They have matcha cookies here.

223
00:12:40,924 --> 00:12:42,924
Those look delicious!

224
00:12:42,947 --> 00:12:45,818
I'll buy these for my friends.

225
00:12:45,842 --> 00:12:48,875
I'd like to get some tea.

226
00:12:48,898 --> 00:12:50,468
Sounds great!

227
00:12:50,492 --> 00:12:54,059
Let's enjoy some together at the hotel tonight.

228
00:12:54,082 --> 00:12:56,940
Yes, I'm looking forward to it!

229
00:12:56,963 --> 00:12:58,463
Scene 6: Miyajima Trip and Itsukushima Shrine

230
00:12:58,463 --> 00:13:01,630
We've arrived in Hiroshima.

231
00:13:01,653 --> 00:13:04,393
Where should we go next?

232
00:13:04,416 --> 00:13:07,869
Let's head to the ferry terminal.

233
00:13:07,892 --> 00:13:11,359
We'll take a ferry to Miyajima.

234
00:13:11,382 --> 00:13:14,188
How long is the ride?

235
00:13:14,212 --> 00:13:16,145
Is it far?

236
00:13:16,168 --> 00:13:19,218
About 15 minutes.

237
00:13:19,242 --> 00:13:22,842
It's close, so we'll be there in no time.

238
00:13:22,865 --> 00:13:26,198
Riding a ferry is so much fun!

239
00:13:26,221 --> 00:13:29,589
The sea breeze feels amazing.

240
00:13:29,613 --> 00:13:32,946
Yes, the weather is perfect today.

241
00:13:32,969 --> 00:13:36,169
Oh, look!

242
00:13:36,192 --> 00:13:40,826
There's something big and red in the water.

243
00:13:40,849 --> 00:13:43,849
That's a torii gate.

244
00:13:43,872 --> 00:13:47,605
It's the torii gate of Itsukushima Shrine.

245
00:13:47,628 --> 00:13:50,037
A torii gate?

246
00:13:50,061 --> 00:13:53,907
Is the shrine in the middle of the sea?

247
00:13:53,930 --> 00:13:55,864
Yes, let’s.

248
00:13:55,887 --> 00:13:59,620
That shrine is actually in the sea.

249
00:13:59,643 --> 00:14:02,695
That's so fascinating!

250
00:14:02,718 --> 00:14:06,052
How do we get inside?

251
00:14:06,074 --> 00:14:14,085
The shrine buildings are also on the water, so we walk across the bridge to enter.

252
00:14:14,109 --> 00:14:17,206
Can we go near the torii gate?

253
00:14:17,230 --> 00:14:21,263
Not right now, since it's in the water.

254
00:14:21,286 --> 00:14:25,983
But in the evening, we can walk out to it.

255
00:14:26,007 --> 00:14:29,880
Wait, we can walk out there?

256
00:14:29,903 --> 00:14:31,970
Why is that?

257
00:14:31,993 --> 00:14:36,531
The water level drops in the evening.

258
00:14:36,555 --> 00:14:40,053
That's why we can walk out to it.

259
00:14:40,076 --> 00:14:43,486
That's amazing!

260
00:14:43,510 --> 00:14:47,723
Let's walk out to it in the evening.

261
00:14:47,746 --> 00:14:50,325
Yes, let's go!

262
00:14:50,349 --> 00:14:54,244
Oh, we've arrived at Miyajima!

263
00:14:54,267 --> 00:14:57,403
Wow, there are so many people here!

264
00:14:57,427 --> 00:15:01,040
Oh, there are deer here too!

265
00:15:01,063 --> 00:15:03,270
Wow, you’re right!

266
00:15:03,293 --> 00:15:07,027
Just like Nara, there are so many deer.

267
00:15:07,050 --> 00:15:10,549
I want to feed them some rice crackers.

268
00:15:10,572 --> 00:15:12,645
Can I buy some?

269
00:15:12,669 --> 00:15:18,546
Please do not feed the deer here.

270
00:15:18,569 --> 00:15:20,069
Scene 7: Himeji Castle – The White Heron Castle

271
00:15:20,069 --> 00:15:23,349
We've arrived in Himeji.

272
00:15:23,372 --> 00:15:26,938
That must be Himeji Castle.

273
00:15:26,961 --> 00:15:31,233
Wow, it's such a massive castle!

274
00:15:31,257 --> 00:15:34,947
And it's so white!

275
00:15:34,970 --> 00:15:39,063
Yes, it's beautiful and so white.

276
00:15:39,087 --> 00:15:43,620
This castle has a special name.

277
00:15:43,643 --> 00:15:46,876
A special name?

278
00:15:46,899 --> 00:15:48,699
What is it?

279
00:15:48,722 --> 00:15:52,008
It's called the White Heron Castle.

280
00:15:52,032 --> 00:15:54,710
White Heron?

281
00:15:54,733 --> 00:15:57,169
What are those?

282
00:15:57,193 --> 00:16:00,860
It's the name of a white bird.

283
00:16:00,883 --> 00:16:03,899
A castle named after a white bird?

284
00:16:03,922 --> 00:16:06,489
What a lovely name!

285
00:16:06,512 --> 00:16:10,845
Now, let's go inside the castle.

286
00:16:10,868 --> 00:16:13,725
Okay, let's go!

287
00:16:13,749 --> 00:16:17,316
Please take off your shoes here.

288
00:16:17,339 --> 00:16:19,272
Got it!

289
00:16:19,295 --> 00:16:22,695
We'll head up from here.

290
00:16:22,718 --> 00:16:26,537
There are so many stairs!

291
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:30,760
Yes, please be careful.

292
00:16:30,783 --> 00:16:32,633
Thank you!

293
00:16:32,657 --> 00:16:36,190
There's still more to go.

294
00:16:36,213 --> 00:16:40,180
Phew, I'm a little tired.

295
00:16:40,203 --> 00:16:42,446
Are you okay?

296
00:16:42,469 --> 00:16:47,103
Yes, but these stairs are long.

297
00:16:47,126 --> 00:16:53,092
It's an old building, so there's no elevator.

298
00:16:53,115 --> 00:16:57,315
You're right. Let's take it slow.

299
00:16:57,338 --> 00:17:02,272
We're almost at the top.

300
00:17:02,295 --> 00:17:04,108
I'll do my best!

301
00:17:04,131 --> 00:17:06,221
We made it!

302
00:17:06,245 --> 00:17:09,521
This is the top.

303
00:17:09,545 --> 00:17:12,145
Look outside.

304
00:17:12,168 --> 00:17:15,340
The view is amazing!

305
00:17:15,363 --> 00:17:20,096
You can see the whole city of Himeji.

306
00:17:20,119 --> 00:17:23,553
The breeze feels so nice.

307
00:17:23,576 --> 00:17:26,948
Are you still tired?

308
00:17:26,972 --> 00:17:32,629
No, seeing this view has re-energized me!

309
00:17:32,653 --> 00:17:36,058
I’m glad to hear that!

310
00:17:36,081 --> 00:17:38,817
Let's take a photo here.

311
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:40,929
Sounds great!

312
00:17:40,953 --> 00:17:44,120
Please stand near the window.

313
00:17:44,143 --> 00:17:46,478
Okay, sure.

314
00:17:46,501 --> 00:17:48,710
I'll take the photo.

315
00:17:48,734 --> 00:17:52,135
Alright, say cheese!

316
00:17:52,159 --> 00:17:54,092
Thank you!

317
00:17:54,115 --> 00:17:56,848
That's a great photo.

318
00:17:56,871 --> 00:17:58,371
Scene 8: Shirakawa-go – The Village of Gassho-Style Houses

319
00:17:58,371 --> 00:18:02,005
What photo are you looking at?

320
00:18:02,028 --> 00:18:05,594
It's a photo of Shirakawa-go in Gifu.

321
00:18:05,617 --> 00:18:09,472
Wow, there's so much snow!

322
00:18:09,496 --> 00:18:14,462
Yes, it snows a lot here in winter.

323
00:18:14,485 --> 00:18:17,290
This village is so beautiful!

324
00:18:17,314 --> 00:18:22,281
Yes, it's also a UNESCO World Heritage site in Japan.

325
00:18:22,304 --> 00:18:25,737
What kind of place is Shirakawa-go?

326
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:29,760
It's an old village nestled in the mountains.

327
00:18:29,783 --> 00:18:33,583
That’s a really large roof, isn’t it?

328
00:18:33,606 --> 00:18:38,292
Yes, it’s called *gassho-zukuri*.

329
00:18:38,315 --> 00:18:42,482
*Gassho-zukuri*? What does that mean?

330
00:18:42,505 --> 00:18:45,372
It means 'hands joined in prayer'—the shape of the roof.

331
00:18:45,395 --> 00:18:47,761
That’s fascinating!

332
00:18:47,784 --> 00:18:50,992
Why is it built this way?

333
00:18:51,016 --> 00:18:55,583
Because it snows a lot here. This shape helps the snow slide off easily.

334
00:18:55,606 --> 00:19:00,073
Ah, I see! The snow just slides right off.

335
00:19:00,096 --> 00:19:03,929
Exactly. It’s the wisdom of the people from long ago.

336
00:19:03,952 --> 00:19:08,386
Who built these houses?

337
00:19:08,409 --> 00:19:11,895
The villagers worked together to build them.

338
00:19:11,918 --> 00:19:14,005
That’s amazing!

339
00:19:14,028 --> 00:19:16,994
Do people still live in them?

340
00:19:17,017 --> 00:19:21,184
Yes, many people still live in them today.

341
00:19:21,207 --> 00:19:24,574
Can we go inside?

342
00:19:24,597 --> 00:19:28,936
Yes, some of them are open for visitors.

343
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:31,893
What’s it like inside?

344
00:19:31,916 --> 00:19:34,729
You’ll find traditional tools and artifacts.

345
00:19:34,753 --> 00:19:36,886
And it’s surprisingly spacious!

346
00:19:36,909 --> 00:19:39,717
That sounds amazing!

347
00:19:39,741 --> 00:19:43,776
In winter, they light up the houses at night.

348
00:19:43,799 --> 00:19:46,168
They light them up?

349
00:19:46,192 --> 00:19:50,592
Yes, the glow from the houses is absolutely beautiful.

350
00:19:50,615 --> 00:19:52,949
That sounds so romantic!

351
00:19:52,972 --> 00:19:56,055
Do you have any photos?

352
00:19:56,078 --> 00:19:58,844
Here, take a look at this one.

353
00:19:58,867 --> 00:20:01,506
Wow, it’s stunning!

354
00:20:01,530 --> 00:20:04,297
I really want to go!

355
00:20:04,320 --> 00:20:07,754
Then let’s go together sometime!

356
00:20:07,777 --> 00:20:09,944
When would be a good time?

357
00:20:09,967 --> 00:20:12,600
Winter would be perfect.

358
00:20:12,623 --> 00:20:15,257
But it’s so cold!

359
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:18,752
What kind of clothes should we wear?

360
00:20:18,775 --> 00:20:22,671
You’ll need a warm coat and boots.

361
00:20:22,695 --> 00:20:24,301
Got it!

362
00:20:24,325 --> 00:20:27,491
Is there any good food to try?

363
00:20:27,514 --> 00:20:30,181
Hida beef is famous here.

364
00:20:30,205 --> 00:20:32,498
It’s delicious Wagyu beef!

365
00:20:32,521 --> 00:20:34,293
Sounds great!

366
00:20:34,317 --> 00:20:37,009
I can’t wait to go!

367
00:20:37,032 --> 00:20:39,266
I’m really looking forward to it!

368
00:20:39,289 --> 00:20:40,789
Scene 9: Exploring Yakushima

369
00:20:40,789 --> 00:20:45,226
Where would you like to travel next?

370
00:20:45,249 --> 00:20:50,900
I’d love to visit Yakushima in Kagoshima.

371
00:20:50,924 --> 00:20:53,291
Yakushima?

372
00:20:53,314 --> 00:20:56,047
What’s it like there?

373
00:20:56,070 --> 00:21:00,803
It’s a stunning island with beautiful mountains and ocean.

374
00:21:00,826 --> 00:21:04,160
It’s also a World Heritage site, right?

375
00:21:04,183 --> 00:21:09,183
Yes, the nature there is breathtaking.

376
00:21:09,206 --> 00:21:13,062
Have you been to Yakushima before?

377
00:21:13,085 --> 00:21:16,574
No, I haven’t.

378
00:21:16,597 --> 00:21:20,597
That’s why I want to go someday!

379
00:21:20,620 --> 00:21:24,100
What can you see in Yakushima?

380
00:21:24,124 --> 00:21:28,741
There's a very old and massive tree.

381
00:21:28,764 --> 00:21:31,611
A huge tree?

382
00:21:31,635 --> 00:21:36,251
Yes, it's a famous cedar tree.

383
00:21:36,274 --> 00:21:39,074
How old is it?

384
00:21:39,097 --> 00:21:42,747
It's thousands of years old.

385
00:21:42,770 --> 00:21:45,945
That's amazing!

386
00:21:45,969 --> 00:21:49,176
I'd love to see it.

387
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:54,233
But it's quite a hike to get to the tree.

388
00:21:54,256 --> 00:21:56,789
How long is the hike?

389
00:21:56,812 --> 00:22:00,979
About 10 hours of mountain hiking.

390
00:22:01,002 --> 00:22:04,813
Wait, 10 hours?

391
00:22:04,836 --> 00:22:07,870
That sounds tough.

392
00:22:07,893 --> 00:22:13,326
Yes, so preparation is key.

393
00:22:13,349 --> 00:22:16,433
What kind of preparation do we need?

394
00:22:16,456 --> 00:22:21,467
First, you'll need comfortable hiking shoes.

395
00:22:21,490 --> 00:22:24,124
Mountain boots, right?

396
00:22:24,147 --> 00:22:26,480
Got it!

397
00:22:26,503 --> 00:22:30,382
And rain gear is a must too.

398
00:22:30,406 --> 00:22:32,872
A raincoat, you mean?

399
00:22:32,895 --> 00:22:35,262
Why is that?

400
00:22:35,285 --> 00:22:40,095
Yakushima gets a lot of rain.

401
00:22:40,118 --> 00:22:42,958
Does it rain often?

402
00:22:42,982 --> 00:22:50,037
Yes, they say it rains 35 days a month.

403
00:22:50,061 --> 00:22:53,227
That sounds amazing!

404
00:22:53,250 --> 00:22:56,227
That's a lot!

405
00:22:56,251 --> 00:23:02,510
Umbrellas are dangerous in the mountains since you need your hands free.

406
00:23:02,533 --> 00:23:04,100
It really is.

407
00:23:04,123 --> 00:23:07,856
Then I'll buy some rain gear.

408
00:23:07,879 --> 00:23:12,112
Let's go shopping together on my day off.

409
00:23:12,135 --> 00:23:14,302
Thank you!

410
00:23:14,325 --> 00:23:17,820
Let's plan to go together sometime.

411
00:23:17,843 --> 00:23:19,610
Yes, let’s.

412
00:23:19,633 --> 00:23:22,803
I'll start exercising a lot from now on.

413
00:23:22,827 --> 00:23:25,261
Let's do our best!

414
00:23:25,284 --> 00:23:26,784
Scene 10: The Nature of Shiretoko – A World Heritage Site

415
00:23:26,784 --> 00:23:29,673
Take a look at the TV.

416
00:23:29,697 --> 00:23:33,772
They're showing a program about Hokkaido.

417
00:23:33,796 --> 00:23:38,929
Wow, the sea and mountains are so beautiful!

418
00:23:38,952 --> 00:23:43,352
Yes, this is Shiretoko.

419
00:23:43,375 --> 00:23:46,775
It's a World Heritage Site in Japan.

420
00:23:46,798 --> 00:23:49,131
Shiretoko?

421
00:23:49,154 --> 00:23:52,688
There's so much nature here.

422
00:23:52,711 --> 00:23:54,487
Yes, let’s.

423
00:23:54,510 --> 00:23:57,076
Oh, look!

424
00:23:57,099 --> 00:23:59,068
There are bears.

425
00:23:59,092 --> 00:24:01,170
Wow, you’re right!

426
00:24:01,194 --> 00:24:03,827
They're huge!

427
00:24:03,850 --> 00:24:07,590
Bears catch fish from the river.

428
00:24:07,613 --> 00:24:10,909
There are so many fish in the river!

429
00:24:10,932 --> 00:24:12,665
Yes, let’s.

430
00:24:12,688 --> 00:24:15,865
Now there's a fox!

431
00:24:15,889 --> 00:24:18,108
It's so cute!

432
00:24:18,131 --> 00:24:21,198
Are there a lot of foxes too?

433
00:24:21,221 --> 00:24:22,821
Yes, let’s.

434
00:24:22,844 --> 00:24:25,711
There are many in the mountains.

435
00:24:25,734 --> 00:24:28,903
And birds are flying in the sky!

436
00:24:28,926 --> 00:24:32,800
Shiretoko is full of wildlife.

437
00:24:32,823 --> 00:24:35,990
It's an amazing place.

438
00:24:36,013 --> 00:24:41,246
I love animals. Me too!

439
00:24:41,269 --> 00:24:44,039
What's Shiretoko like in winter?

440
00:24:44,063 --> 00:24:47,359
It snows a lot in winter.

441
00:24:47,382 --> 00:24:50,149
It gets very cold.

442
00:24:50,172 --> 00:24:52,544
What happens to the ocean?

443
00:24:52,568 --> 00:24:56,622
Lots of white ice drifts into the sea.

444
00:24:56,645 --> 00:24:59,279
White ice?

445
00:24:59,302 --> 00:25:01,272
Yes, let’s.

446
00:25:01,295 --> 00:25:04,030
It comes from the distant northern seas.

447
00:25:04,053 --> 00:25:06,488
That’s amazing!

448
00:25:06,512 --> 00:25:10,078
Are there animals on the ice?

449
00:25:10,101 --> 00:25:11,968
Yes, let’s.

450
00:25:11,991 --> 00:25:17,124
You’ll see white birds and seals on the ice.

451
00:25:17,147 --> 00:25:20,681
Can we see the ice from the ship?

452
00:25:20,704 --> 00:25:22,353
Yes, let’s.

453
00:25:22,376 --> 00:25:26,450
We’ll sail close to the ice.

454
00:25:26,474 --> 00:25:29,341
That sounds exciting!

455
00:25:29,364 --> 00:25:32,617
It’s very popular, you know.

456
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:36,207
I’d love to visit Shiretoko someday.

457
00:25:36,230 --> 00:25:38,110
Sounds great!

458
00:25:38,134 --> 00:25:41,471
And the food there is delicious too!

459
00:25:41,494 --> 00:25:43,788
What’s good to eat?

460
00:25:43,811 --> 00:25:48,745
The seafood—fish and crab—are absolutely amazing.

461
00:25:48,768 --> 00:25:50,426
I want to try it!

462
00:25:50,449 --> 00:25:52,920
How do we get there?

463
00:25:52,944 --> 00:25:57,477
Fly from Tokyo to Hokkaido.

464
00:25:57,500 --> 00:26:00,434
Then take a bus?

465
00:26:00,457 --> 00:26:02,072
Yes, let’s.

466
00:26:02,095 --> 00:26:05,065
Yes, the bus takes you to Shiretoko.

467
00:26:05,089 --> 00:26:07,455
It’s a bit far.

468
00:26:07,478 --> 00:26:11,812
It’s far, but I *have* to go someday.

469
00:26:11,834 --> 00:26:14,568
Let’s go together sometime!

470
00:26:14,591 --> 00:26:16,157
Yes, let’s.

471
00:26:16,180 --> 00:26:20,314
That wraps up our lesson on Japan’s World Heritage sites.

472
00:26:20,337 --> 00:26:24,103
We’ve made so many travel plans!

473
00:26:24,126 --> 00:26:27,693
I want to visit all these places someday.